            p("Take a food-delivery app. From far away it is a handful of services, such as orders, couriers and payments, each with its own data, talking through an API gateway and a stream of events. Up close, each of those boxes is a program of its own, with modules, tables and rules. System design works at both distances. The far view is high-level design (HLD), and the close view is low-level design (LLD)."),
            p("The C4 model makes the same point with a set of hierarchical diagrams: the system context, its containers, the components inside a container, and finally the code [[c4]]. Neither level is more real. They answer different questions for different readers, and they change at different speeds."),
